Holiday tables contain factual calendar dates. Calendar identities, verified
and projected horizons, primary sources, and independent validation scope are
documented in SPEC.md. The source repository pins development references in
tests/requirements.txt; generated provenance and comparison evidence are written
under target/test-results/. Development reference artifacts are not shipped in
the crates.io archive.

The development oracle uses QuantLib, FinancePy, Python holidays and supporting
Python packages. The Rust library does not bundle or link these implementations;
it has no runtime dependencies. No upstream implementation source is vendored.
